{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/766022-dark-ages-fera","id":766022,"title":"Dark Ages Fera","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-14T20:23:57-08:00","id":766022,"title":"Dark Ages Fera","content":"Hello,<br /> <br /> something I was wondering about the other day is what were the various Changing Breeds, or Fera, up to during the medieval period? Werewolf the dark ages covers well just the werewolves for the most part. So I am curious what the various different changing breeds were like and how they might have been different during the middle ages?<br /> <br /> ~herkles~","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T05:38:44-08:00","id":766190,"title":"","content":"Well, travel is a lot harder, so you wouldn't see much variety, especially as you move away from the Mediterranean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T07:56:50-08:00","id":768503,"title":"","content":"If we are talking strictly in Europe and the Mediterranean, here's how I would handle Fera in the Dark Ages. The Crusades and the Moorish occupation of the Iberian peninsula offer greater incidence of crossover of breeds, but since there is not yet an Ahadi in Africa yet, there is little common ground or cooperation amongst the breeds--no contact with the Hengeyokai either. A recurring theme among any Fera is going to be staying hidden from the Garou.<br /> <br /> Bastet: The Ceilican are still active across Europe, probably most active in pagan corners of the continent or cultivating antipathy for the Church. The Bubasti are certainly active in Egypt and elsewhere in Northern Africa. The African and Middle Eastern tribes may pop up occasionally in the Iberian Peninsula or the Levant, but they are not widely known.<br /> <br /> Corax: Widely present throughout Europe. Some of the least affected by the War of Rage. Good candidates for crossover with Garou or other breeds of Fera, given their nosy natures--plus, much easier to travel when you can fly AND know all the shortcuts in the Umbra.<br /> <br /> Gurahl: All in hibernation still. There could be a Great-grandmother or -grandfather that's awake and active in Europe, though, but likely keeping a low profile.<br /> <br /> Ananasi: Probably hiding throughout Europe, but off doing their own thing.<br /> <br /> Rokea: Very, very few Betweeners. Like the Ananasi, generally off doing their own thing under the sea.<br /> <br /> Ratkin: Active in cities. Almost certainly have a hand in the various waves of the Black Death (and other pestilences) that spread across Europe. Brown rat arrives in Europe at some point during the Middles Ages--could be some interesting crossover between different &quot;Plagues&quot; of Ratkin, i.e. the European Gamine vs. the arrival of The Horde. Possibly no Freak Aspects yet.<br /> <br /> Nagah: Policing the Garou and Fera from the shadows, as usual.<br /> <br /> Mokole: Small population in Egypt, chilling out with their mnesis and generally keeping out the way.<br /> <br /> Ajaba: Busy fighting amongst themselves in Africa.<br /> <br /> Nuwisha, Kitsune: None in Europe.<br /> <br /> Grondr, Apis, Camazotz: extinct in Europe as of the Dark Ages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9475-worldlycannibal","name":"worldlycannibal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}